"\\\"JASPER\\\"\" | \"\\\"KESTREL\\\"\" | \"\\\"LUMEN\\\"\" | \"\\\"MOSAIC\\\"\" | \"\\\"NEXUS\\\"\")\nresponse-format-2-source-id-kv ::= \"\\\"source_id\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-2-source-id\nresponse-format-2-start-line ::= ([1-9] [0-9]{0,15})\nresponse-format-2-start-line-kv ::= \"\\\"start_line\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-2-start-line\nresponse-format-3 ::= \"{\" space response-format-3-action-kv \",\" space response-format-3-requests-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-3-action ::= \"\\\"read_batch\\\"\"\nresponse-format-3-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-3-action\nresponse-format-3-requests ::= \"[\" space response-format-3-requests-item (\",\" space response-format-3-requests-item)? space \"]\"\nresponse-format-3-requests-item ::= \"{\" space response-format-3-requests-item-end-line-kv \",\" space response-format-3-requests-item-source-id-kv \",\" space response-format-3-requests-item-start-line-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-3-requests-item-end-line ::= ([1-9] [0-9]{0,15})\nresponse-format-3-requests-item-end-line-kv ::= \"\\\"end_line\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-3-requests-item-end-line\nresponse-format-3-requests-item-source-id ::= (\"\\\"AURORA\\\"\" | \"\\\"BASTION\\\"\" | \"\\\"CIPHER\\\"\" | \"\\\"DELTA\\\"\" | \"\\\"ECHO\\\"\" | \"\\\"FALCON\\\"\" | \"\\\"GARNET\\\"\" | \"\\\"HELIX\\\"\" | \"\\\"INDIGO\\\"\" | \"\\\"JASPER\\\"\" | \"\\\"KESTREL\\\"\" | \"\\\"LUMEN\\\"\" | \"\\\"MOSAIC\\\"\" | \"\\\"NEXUS\\\"\")\nresponse-format-3-requests-item-source-id-kv ::= \"\\\"source_id\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-3-requests-item-source-id\nresponse-format-3-requests-item-start-line ::= ([1-9] [0-9]{0,15})\nresponse-format-3-requests-item-start-line-kv ::= \"\\\"start_line\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-3-requests-item-start-line\nresponse-format-3-requests-kv ::= \"\\\"requests\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-3-requests\nresponse-format-4 ::= \"{\" space response-format-4-action-kv \",\" space response-format-4-result-id-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-4-action ::= \"\\\"reopen_exact\\\"\"\nresponse-format-4-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-action\nresponse-format-4-result-id ::= (\"\\\"RESULT-001\\\"\" | \"\\\"RESULT-002\\\"\" | \"\\\"RESULT-003\\\"\" | \"\\\"RESULT-004\\\"\" | \"\\\"RESULT-005\\\"\")\nresponse-format-4-result-id-kv ::= \"\\\"result_id\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-result-id\nresponse-format-5 ::= \"{\" space response-format-5-action-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-5-action ::= \"\\\"submit\\\"\"\nresponse-format-5-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-5-action\nroot ::= \"<|im_start|>assistant\\n\" (\"<think>\" space until-5 (\"</think>\" | ))? space response-format\nspace ::= | \" \" | \"\\n\"{1,2} [ \\t]{0,20}\nstring ::= \"\\\"\" char* \"\\\"\"\nuntil-5 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<] until-5\nuntil-5-01 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [/] until-5-02 | [t] until-5-09 | [^/<t] until-5\nuntil-5-02 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [t] until-5-03 | [^<t] until-5\nuntil-5-03 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [h] until-5-04 | [^<h] until-5\nuntil-5-04 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [i] until-5-05 | [^<i] until-5\nuntil-5-05 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [n] until-5-06 | [^<n] until-5\nuntil-5-06 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [k] until-5-07 | [^<k] until-5\nuntil-5-07 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\nuntil-5-09 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-10 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-10 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-11 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-11 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-12 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-12 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [_] until-5-13 | [^<_] until-5\nuntil-5-13 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [c] until-5-14 | [^<c] until-5\nuntil-5-14 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [a] until-5-15 | [^<a] until-5\nuntil-5-15 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-16 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-16 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-17 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-17 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\n","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\nYou are the ordinary actor responsible for exact task work in a bounded context. Use only declared actions. Exact sources, candidates, observations, effects, and checks are externally custodied and reopenable. Semantic residue, when present, is lossy, incomplete, non-authoritative, and never a substitute for exact verification or independent readiness. Return exactly one action object per decision.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task — Solace regional-water recovery decision\n\nSolace County must restore a regional drinking-water network after wildfire,\npower, treatment, hydraulic, and control-system disturbances. Build and maintain\nthe exact candidate files, then propose submission only when the package is\ngenuinely ready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains fourteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nCatalog titles help navigation but do not supply findings. Read the bytes needed\nfor the work and cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a compact task-native evidence and\ndecision matrix. Preserve source-bound facts, cross-source dependencies,\nconflicts, unknowns, candidate currency, and citations. This exact artifact is\nnon-authoritative but may carry cumulative work across context turnover.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,500–2,100-word Solace\nWater Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section headings. Use at\nleast eleven distinct source IDs and integrate—not merely list—the governing\nrelationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — incident, utility, public-health, communication, and closure authority;\n- Q02 — pressure, storage, isolation, residence time, and candidate-bound hydraulics;\n- Q03 — sampling rounds, spacing, detection limits, action thresholds, and staleness;\n- Q04 — pump capacity, shared-main limits, staged demand, and current evidence;\n- Q05 — grid, generator, fuel, staffing, chemicals, and resource contingencies;\n- Q06 — treatment barriers, turbidity, disinfectant, source blend, and contact time;\n- Q07 — contamination hypotheses, observations, locations, investigation holds, and falsifiers;\n- Q08 — access, token and key state, immutable custody, retention, and automation restoration;\n- Q09 — telemetry coverage, warnings versus actions, delays, alternates, and uncertainty;\n- Q10 — environmental determination, notice clock, permits, discharge, and evidence custody;\n- Q11 — public advisories, accessibility, alternate water, service states, and communications;\n- Q12 — candidate lineage, rollback, effect uptake, current checks, blockers, independent readiness, and closure.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve psi versus kPa, gallons versus treated reserve, micrograms versus\nmilligrams, reporting limits versus action thresholds, percentages versus\nmeasured concentration, rated versus usable power, nameplate versus shared\ncapacity, warnings versus isolation triggers, forecast versus observation, and\nmechanical checks versus public-health and independent readiness. Candidate,\nhydraulic, sampling, treatment, pump, power, key, role, telemetry, or source-\nwater changes can make earlier evidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timing, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, rollback and retirement conditions, and\nevidence that would falsify important claims. Do not infer that a provenance\nrecord, mutation, green check, or submission establishes readiness.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Solace Verification-Frame Action Contract\n\nReturn exactly one JSON action object and no prose.\n\nThe current candidate and its latest admitted effect are already visible. Begin by checking the current candidate. Use the candidate-bound findings to make bounded repairs, recheck after every candidate change, and submit only when the current check passes and external readiness adjudication remains the only unresolved authority.\n\nAllowed actions:\n\n```json\n{\"action\":\"patch_decision\",\"edits\":[{\"old\":\"exact unique current text\",\"new\":\"replacement text\"}]}\n{\"action\":\"run_check\"}\n{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":20}\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":20},{\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":20}]}\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-...\"}\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}\n```\n\n`patch_decision` is a bounded exact edit operation. It permits 1–24 edits, requires every `old` anchor to occur exactly once in the current decision, limits each old anchor to 2,000 UTF-8 bytes, and limits all replacement text in one action to 12,000 UTF-8 bytes. It does not authorize semantic repair by the host; the actor chooses every edit.\n\nSource reads and exact reopens remain available when the candidate-bound findings require exact evidence. The source catalog gives the valid line bounds.\n\nA successful patch makes every earlier check stale. `run_check` binds its findings to one exact candidate hash. A passed mechanical check does not itself authorize operational recovery or prove independent readiness.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"debbe3de17dc0511fe3b9f5be920a83367c84efaedb34ef4095a9add315a0761\",\"size_bytes\":4111,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"title\":\"Emergency authority and restoration accountability\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"f0a85d8273e5058984554a6383d51616f2e103f141b7e268f67215b90fc7ed60\",\"size_bytes\":3483,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"title\":\"Hydraulic pressure, storage, and zone isolation evidence\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"size_bytes\":3991,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"title\":\"Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"size_bytes\":4013,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"title\":\"Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"a3826feabfb2389ef861bba819d3ae178c9e9086a8f309722ba1413591ff8395\",\"size_bytes\":3565,\"source_id\":\"ECHO\",\"title\":\"Grid, generator, and fuel continuity\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"62997706c361243e5d2720ccc088b53d3bcc2c64e64e6ee054d588aeac8fd8b8\",\"size_bytes\":3344,\"source_id\":\"FALCON\",\"title\":\"Treatment barriers, disinfectant, and turbidity controls\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"b9451cc48b50a436eefd497a4dbf5ac4974431ad0f07f9bb79796709584ab0fb\",\"size_bytes\":3622,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"title\":\"Source-water contamination hypotheses and watershed controls\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"dcb5a4ce70bf47372c5a52a096e89f890c74f7be1363fd78dfaf9c6cd10536e5\",\"size_bytes\":3386,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"title\":\"Access, control-system integrity, and evidence custody\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"64836aa42ff09665cee35507acf1ca8f242ddb78ed4457b0e81e31a93c9c8977\",\"size_bytes\":3704,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"title\":\"Telemetry coverage, alerts, and observation quality\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"feaaeb0601ea46b069dff02673e85774d86ff857def778cc48ecc0f6df706e00\",\"size_bytes\":3310,\"source_id\":\"JASPER\",\"title\":\"Environmental permits, discharge, and reporting\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"2536c9c9d966266ccfecd69690d7575dcb4025b53ab52812cece766b0077c600\",\"size_bytes\":3584,\"source_id\":\"KESTREL\",\"title\":\"Fuel, chemicals, staffing, and mutual-aid logistics\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"1a50bae39974b3c33c2a0a6b6b94859b75f41e3c4d4a01f17cf519db7b98253c\",\"size_bytes\":3813,\"source_id\":\"LUMEN\",\"title\":\"Public warnings, accessibility, and customer continuity\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"a3836321537dc4f3ee3cacc094761d5176c0a7f08ae891f4fc4e1ee5b3f84b4d\",\"size_bytes\":3861,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"title\":\"Candidate lineage, rollback, and configuration control\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"85aabce45a9704e4f55ee1418528eb083a7c46326dbb366b0cb4a3ddcd9df0d6\",\"size_bytes\":3762,\"source_id\":\"NEXUS\",\"title\":\"Independent readiness review, blockers, and falsifiers\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"candidate_sha256\":\"82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v008:82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"files\":{\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\":\"0fd482aff52c6919049709d28c74f07bc9be915b2c77595f68dc0637db6cb1a6\",\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\":\"bcc9d7f537633744508752c123cb95d4f0c460bfb954a6771a4fa1ad6ec15bea\"},\"schema\":\"architecture-current-candidate-v0\"}\n--- exact candidate file: EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md ---\n# Solace Evidence and Decision Matrix\n\n| ID | Domain | Source | Fact/Observation | Unit/Value | Status | Dependencies | Conflicts/Unknowns | Candidate Currency | Citations |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| E-01 | Authority | AURORA | County health officer lifts do-not-drink only after current lab/distribution verification | n/a | Active | CIPHER, BASTION | Utility repair ≠ public-health authorization | W7 | [AURORA] |\n| E-02 | Authority | AURORA | Final closure requires utility director acceptance of all blockers/risks | n/a | Active | NEXUS | Residual risk must be explicit | W7 | [AURORA] |\n| E-03 | Hydraulic | BASTION | Min distribution pressure north zone | 42 psi | Current | DELTA, ECHO | Warning 38 psi vs Isolation 30 psi distinct | W7/H12 | [BASTION] |\n| E-04 | Hydraulic | BASTION | Ridge storage volume / 12-hr emergency reserve | 5.8M gal / 3.2M gal | Current | DELTA | Gallons vs treated reserve distinct | W7/H12 | [BASTION] |\n| E-05 | Sampling | CIPHER | Clearance requires two complete rounds ≥16 hours apart | n/a | Active | BASTION, GARNET | One clean round insufficient | W7 | [CIPHER] |\n| E-06 | Sampling | CIPHER | Benzene reporting limit / action threshold | 0.5 µg/L / 5.0 µg/L | Current | GARNET | Reporting limit ≠ action threshold; µg/L not mg/L | W7 | [CIPHER] |\n| E-07 | Pump | DELTA | Pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power | n/a | Active | BASTION, ECHO | Cavitation constraints apply | W7/P9 | [DELTA] |\n| E-08 | Power | ECHO | Emergency generation capacity/duration | 4.1 MW / 36 hrs | Current | KESTREL | Excludes mobile-pump load; not 36 days | W7 | [ECHO] |\n| E-09 | Power | ECHO | Grid feed rated vs usable power | 8.2 MW rated / 6.5 MW usable | Current | DELTA | Damaged switchgear limits delivery | W7 | [ECHO] |\n| E-10 | Treatment | FALCON | Free chlorine entry vs distribution thresholds | 0.8–2.0 mg/L entry / ≥0.2 mg/L dist | Current | INDIGO | Entry and distribution controls distinct; mg/L not µg/L | W7/T6 | [FALCON] |\n| E-11 | Treatment | FALCON | Combined-filter turbidity current vs release gate | 0.18 NTU / ≤0.30 NTU (4 hrs) | Current | INDIGO | 0.18 NTU is not chlorine residual | W7/T6 | [FALCON] |\n| E-12 | Source | GARNET | Ash-plume intake impact probability next rain | 34% forecast | Active | CIPHER, FALCON | Forecast probability ≠ measured contamination; reservoir vs river intake distinct | W7 | [GARNET] |\n| E-13 | Source | GARNET | Chemical yard investigation hold active | n/a | Active | CIPHER | Containment trench not inspected below grade | W7 | [GARNET] |\n| E-14 | Access | HELIX | SCADA token revoked; controller key current (W4) | n/a | Current | INDIGO, MOSAIC | Break-glass expires 2 hrs + dual approval; emergency ≠ continuing auth | W7/W4 | [HELIX] |\n| E-15 | Telemetry | INDIGO | Critical-signal coverage | 96% covered / 4% unobserved | Current | BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON | Coverage ≠ confidence; uninstrumented zones not proven healthy | W7 | [INDIGO] |\n| E-16 | Telemetry | INDIGO | Pressure warning vs isolation trigger | 38 psi warn / 30 psi isolate | Current | BASTION | Warning and action thresholds must remain distinct | W7 | [INDIGO] |\n| E-17 | Environmental | JASPER | Unauthorized discharge notice clock | 72 hours from determination | Active | GARNET, FALCON, LUMEN | Determination event ≠ detection time; AURORA owns materiality | W7 | [JASPER] |\n| E-18 | Environmental | JASPER | Emergency dechlorination residual limit | ≤0.019 mg/L at outfall | Current | FALCON | Immediate stop required if exceeded; permit E-17 | W7 | [JASPER] |\n| E-19 | Logistics | KESTREL | Diesel stock coverage emergency vs full pump load | 36 hrs / 22 hrs | Current | ECHO, DELTA | Load regimes distinct; not days | W7 | [KESTREL] |\n| E-20 | Logistics | KESTREL | Coagulant/chlorine stock duration | 4.5 days / 3.2 days | Current | FALCON | Inventory duration ≠ delivery lead time | W7 | [KESTREL] |\n| E-21 | Public | LUMEN | Do-not-drink notice delivery coverage | 91% registered endpoints | Current | CIPHER, AURORA | Missing 9% is comm uncertainty, not pop reduction | W7 | [LUMEN] |\n| E-22 | Public | LUMEN | Call center capacity vs forecast demand | 3,200/hr (6 hrs) / 4,100/hr forecast | Current | KESTREL | Alternate-language outreach may reduce repeats | W7 | [LUMEN] |\n| E-23 | Change | MOSAIC | Current recovery candidate | W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4) | Current | ALL | W6 evidence historical unless transferred/rechecked | W7 | [MOSAIC] |\n| E-24 | Change | MOSAIC | Rollback to W6 mechanical possibility | Valve map V8 + firmware C11 compatible | Active | BASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX | Mechanical possibility ≠ authorization | W7→W6 | [MOSAIC] |\n| E-25 | Readiness | NEXUS | Open findings count | 16 (5 hyd, 4 treat, 3 samp, 2 pow, 2 comm) | Current | ALL | Finding count ≠ readiness percentage | W7 | [NEXUS] |\n| E-26 | Readiness | NEXUS | Blocking findings | Incomplete 2nd-round samples; stale gen transfer evidence; missing PH duty officer ack | Active | CIPHER, ECHO, AURORA | Independent review required; no self-authorization | W7 | [NEXUS] |\n\n## Cross-Source Dependencies\n- CIPHER sampling consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET hypotheses [CIPHER, BASTION, GARNET].\n- DELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power [DELTA, BASTION, ECHO].\n- FALCON treatment selection depends on GARNET source hypotheses [FALCON, GARNET].\n- INDIGO telemetry supports BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON but each retains own decision gate [INDIGO, BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON].\n- HELIX audit events consumed by INDIGO; HELIX does not authorize access [HELIX, INDIGO].\n- JASPER environmental notices depend on GARNET source impact and FALCON discharge conditions [JASPER, GARNET, FALCON].\n- KESTREL fuel supports ECHO generator duration; KESTREL chemicals support FALCON staging [KESTREL, ECHO, FALCON].\n- LUMEN communications depend on CIPHER/AURORA advisory status and INDIGO/BASTION service observations [LUMEN, CIPHER, AURORA, INDIGO, BASTION].\n- MOSAIC candidate changes make BASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX evidence stale [MOSAIC, BASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX].\n- NEXUS consumes all sources for independent review but does not mutate states [NEXUS, ALL].\n\n## Conflicts and Unknowns\n- GARNET ash-plume 34% is forecast, not observed contamination; reservoir (non-detect) vs river intake (3.1 µg/L) must not be merged [GARNET].\n- Chemical yard investigation hold active; trench inspection below grade pending [GARNET].\n- INDIGO 4% unobserved coverage does not prove healthy uninstrumented zones [INDIGO].\n- HELIX break-glass access expired; remote automation restoration requires named evidence [HELIX].\n- NEXUS blocking findings: second-round samples incomplete, generator transfer evidence stale, PH duty officer acknowledgment missing [NEXUS].\n\n## Candidate Currency\nCurrent candidate W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4) [MOSAIC]. Any mutation to hydraulic model, pump plan, treatment plan, key set, valve map, or firmware makes prior evidence stale and requires recheck [MOSAIC]. Rollback to W6 mechanically possible only with V8/C11 compatibility but not authorized [MOSAIC].\n\n## Falsifiers for Important Claims\n- If CIPHER second-round samples show benzene ≥5.0 µg/L at any location, clearance claim falsified [CIPHER].\n- If ECHO generator transfer evidence remains stale after recheck, 36-hr duration claim falsified [ECHO].\n- If AURORA public-health duty officer does not acknowledge, closure claim falsified [AURORA].\n- If FALCON turbidity exceeds 0.30 NTU for >4 hrs, release gate claim falsified [FALCON].\n- If INDIGO coverage drops below 96% or unobserved zones show adverse conditions, telemetry adequacy claim falsified [INDIGO].\n--- exact candidate file: BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md ---\n# Solace Water Recovery Decision\n\n## Authority, scope, and restoration decision\nThe Solace County Water Recovery Decision is governed by the authority that only the county health officer may lift a do-not-drink order, and only after current laboratory and distribution-system verification; a utility repair or green mechanical check is not public-health authorization [AURORA]. Final closure requires the utility director to accept every declared blocker and residual risk [AURORA]. BASTION and CIPHER supply hydraulic and laboratory evidence but cannot lift health restrictions [AURORA]. The current recovery candidate is W7 with hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, treatment plan T6, and key set W4; evidence for W6 is historical unless explicitly transferred and rechecked [MOSAIC]. Rollback to W6 is mechanically possible only while valve map V8 and controller firmware C11 remain compatible, but mechanical possibility is not authorization [MOSAIC]. Every mutation must record before and after candidate hashes, changed files, affected evidence, check currency, owner, and rollback effect [MOSAIC].\n\n## Hydraulics, storage, and zone sequencing\nThe north-zone distribution system currently holds a minimum pressure of 42 psi [BASTION]. Ridge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons; these are distinct measures and must not be conflated as treated reserve [BASTION]. DELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power; cavitation constraints limit shared-main capacity under staged demand conditions [DELTA, BASTION, ECHO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states: a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Residence time in the distribution loop must be verified against candidate-bound hydraulic model H12; any change to valve map V8 or controller firmware C11 invalidates prior residence-time evidence [MOSAIC]. The current minimum pressure of 42 psi exceeds the 30 psi isolation trigger but remains within the operational band defined by H12; no isolation action is currently indicated [BASTION, INDIGO].\n\n## Sampling, source water, and treatment barriers\nClearance requires two complete sampling rounds spaced at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient [CIPHER]. The benzene reporting limit is 0.5 micrograms per liter and the action threshold is 5.0 micrograms per liter; these are distinct controls and must not be conflated, as a reporting limit indicates analytical capability while an action threshold triggers public-health response [CIPHER]. CIPHER sample placement consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses; any change to hydraulic routing or source-water characterization makes prior sampling evidence stale [CIPHER, BASTION, GARNET]. Current volatile-organic screening is non-detect at the reservoir and 3.1 micrograms per liter at the river intake; these locations must not be merged, as they represent distinct hydrological positions with different contamination probabilities [GARNET]. The ash-plume model assigns a 34 percent chance of intake impact during the next rain event, which is a forecast probability, not measured contamination [GARNET]. The investigation hold remains active for the chemical yard because the containment trench has not been inspected below grade; this hold blocks clearance until resolved [GARNET]. Staleness applies: any candidate-bound hydraulic, pump, treatment, or source-water change invalidates prior sampling rounds and requires re-sampling per CIPHER protocol [CIPHER, MOSAIC].\n\n## Power, pumping, logistics, and demand stages\nEmergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock; the duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load [ECHO]. The grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW; rated power is not usable power [ECHO]. KESTREL diesel stock covers emergency load for 36 hours and full pump load for 22 hours; these load regimes are distinct and must not be merged as a single duration [KESTREL, ECHO]. Coagulant and chlorine chemical stocks provide 4.5 days and 3.2 days of treatment capacity respectively; inventory duration is not delivery lead time [KESTREL, FALCON]. Staffing continuity depends on mutual-aid logistics; current shift coverage must be verified against the 36-hour generator window [KESTREL]. Any change to ECHO power state or KESTREL fuel stock makes prior pump sequencing evidence stale [DELTA, ECHO, KESTREL]. The shared-main limit under staged demand requires that DELTA pump capacity not exceed the 6.5 MW usable grid feed plus any available generator margin without triggering cavitation constraints [DELTA, ECHO, BASTION].\n\n## Treatment barriers, turbidity, disinfectant, and source blend\nFree chlorine must remain between 0.8 and 2.0 milligrams per liter at entry points and at least 0.2 mg/L in distribution; these are distinct controls with different thresholds and units of measure [FALCON]. Current combined-filter turbidity is 0.18 NTU, with a release gate at or below 0.30 NTU sustained for four hours; the 0.18 NTU value is a turbidity measurement, not a chlorine residual [FALCON]. Source blending must account for GARNET contamination hypotheses: the river intake shows 3.1 µg/L volatile-organics while the reservoir remains non-detect, requiring distinct treatment paths and contact times [GARNET, FALCON]. Treatment plan T6 governs current disinfectant dosing and turbidity controls; any change to source blend or turbidity profile invalidates prior treatment evidence [MOSAIC, FALCON, GARNET]. The emergency dechlorination residual limit at outfall is ≤0.019 mg/L under permit E-17; exceeding this requires immediate stop of discharge [JASPER, FALCON]. Contact time verification must be rechecked after any hydraulic model change to H12 or valve map modification to V8 [MOSAIC, FALCON, BASTION].\n\n## Contamination hypotheses, investigation holds, and falsifiers\nThe ash-plume model assigns a 34 percent chance of intake impact during the next rain event; this is a forecast probability, not observed contamination, and must be distinguished from measured values [GARNET]. Volatile-organic screening shows non-detect at the reservoir and 3.1 µg/L at the river intake; these locations are hydrologically distinct and must not be merged into a single source-water characterization [GARNET]. The chemical yard investigation hold remains active because the containment trench has not been inspected below grade; this hold blocks any claim of complete source-water clearance [GARNET]. Falsifiers for important claims include: if CIPHER second-round samples show benzene ≥5.0 µg/L at any location, the clearance claim is falsified [CIPHER]; if GARNET river-intake measurements exceed 5.0 µg/L after the next rain event, the 34% forecast underestimates actual contamination [GARNET, CIPHER]; if FALCON turbidity exceeds 0.30 NTU for more than four hours, the release gate claim is falsified [FALCON]. Any new observation at the river intake that contradicts the non-detect reservoir value requires re-evaluation of source blending under T6 [GARNET, FALCON, MOSAIC].\n\n## Access, control-system integrity, and evidence custody\nThe exposed SCADA service token was revoked at 14:10 UTC [HELIX]. The controller signing key was not exposed and remains current under key-set version W4; break-glass access expires after two hours and requires dual approval plus immutable session logging, meaning emergency access is not continuing authorization [HELIX]. Online control logs are retained for ninety days and archived incident evidence for seven years; these periods serve different obligations and must not be conflated as a single retention policy [HELIX]. Automation restoration requires named evidence of key integrity, token rotation, and controller firmware state; a green mechanical check does not establish control-system readiness [HELIX, MOSAIC]. Immutable custody of audit events is consumed by INDIGO telemetry but HELIX does not authorize access independently [HELIX, INDIGO]. Any change to key-set W4, valve map V8, or controller firmware C11 invalidates prior access and automation evidence and requires re-verification under MOSAIC lineage rules [MOSAIC, HELIX]. Rollback of control-system state is possible only while V8 and C11 compatibility persists; mechanical rollback does not constitute operational authorization [MOSAIC, HELIX].\n\n## Telemetry coverage, alerts, delays, and uncertainty\nCritical-signal telemetry coverage stands at 96 percent, with 4 percent of monitored points unobserved; this coverage gap does not prove the uninstrumented zones are healthy, only that they are not currently observable [INDIGO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states; a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Telemetry delays in the unobserved 4 percent create uncertainty that must be treated as potential adverse condition until verified by direct observation or alternate telemetry [INDIGO]. Warnings versus actions: a pressure warning at 38 psi requires monitoring and logging but does not require isolation; an isolation trigger at 30 psi requires immediate valve closure and zone separation [INDIGO, BASTION]. Any change to hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, or control-system key set W4 invalidates prior telemetry correlation evidence and requires re-verification of coverage and alert thresholds [MOSAIC, INDIGO, BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON]. Alternate telemetry paths must be identified for the 4 percent unobserved zone before closure can be claimed [INDIGO, NEXUS].\n\n## Environmental determination, notice clock, permits, and discharge\nThe unauthorized discharge notice clock is 72 hours from the determination event, not from detection time; AURORA owns materiality of the determination [JASPER]. The emergency dechlorination residual limit at outfall is ≤0.019 mg/L under permit E-17; exceeding this requires immediate stop of discharge and triggers the notice clock [JASPER, FALCON]. Environmental notices depend on GARNET source impact and FALCON discharge conditions; a change in either invalidates prior environmental evidence [JASPER, GARNET, FALCON]. Evidence custody for environmental records follows HELIX retention: 90 days online, 7 years archived incident evidence [HELIX, JASPER]. The determination event that starts the 72-hour clock must be documented with timestamp, responsible officer, and supporting laboratory or telemetry evidence; a forecast probability from GARNET does not constitute a determination event [JASPER, GARNET, AURORA]. Any discharge exceeding permit limits requires immediate public notification under LUMEN protocols in addition to environmental agency notice [JASPER, LUMEN, FALCON].\n\n## Public advisories, accessibility, alternate water, and communications\nDo-not-drink notice delivery coverage reaches 91 percent of registered endpoints; the missing 9 percent represents communication uncertainty, not a reduction in affected population [LUMEN]. Call center capacity is 3,200 calls per hour for six hours, while forecast demand is 4,100 calls per hour; alternate-language outreach may reduce repeat calls but does not eliminate the gap [LUMEN]. Public advisories depend on CIPHER/AURORA advisory status and INDIGO/BASTION service observations; any change in clearance status or hydraulic state requires immediate re-issuance [LUMEN, CIPHER, AURORA, INDIGO, BASTION]. Accessibility requirements mandate that alternate water sources be identified for the 9 percent unregistered population; this is a service obligation, not a telemetry gap [LUMEN, KESTREL]. Service states must be communicated distinctly: do-not-drink, boil-water, and normal-service are separate public-health states with different required actions [LUMEN, AURORA, CIPHER]. Any change to advisory status requires re-verification of delivery coverage and accessibility compliance before the next communication cycle [LUMEN, MOSAIC].\n\n## Candidate lineage, rollback, effect uptake, checks, blockers, and closure\nCurrent candidate W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4) is the operative recovery state; W6 evidence is historical unless explicitly transferred and rechecked under MOSAIC rules [MOSAIC]. Rollback to W6 is mechanically possible only while valve map V8 and controller firmware C11 remain compatible; mechanical possibility is not authorization [MOSAIC]. Effect uptake: any mutation to hydraulic model, pump plan, treatment plan, key set, valve map, or firmware makes prior evidence stale and requires recheck before any operational decision can be made on the basis of that evidence [MOSAIC, BASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX]. Current checks bind to the exact candidate; any later effect makes the prior check stale and invalidates readiness claims based on that check [MOSAIC, NEXUS]. Blocking findings include: incomplete second-round samples under CIPHER protocol, stale generator transfer evidence under ECHO, and missing public-health duty officer acknowledgment under AURORA [NEXUS, CIPHER, ECHO, AURORA]. Independent readiness review by NEXUS consumes all sources but does not mutate states; no self-authorization of readiness is permitted [NEXUS, AURORA]. Closure requires the utility director to accept every declared blocker and residual risk after independent review confirms that all blocking findings are resolved [AURORA, NEXUS]. Submission of this decision does not establish readiness; it proposes submission for independent review only when the package is genuinely ready [AURORA, NEXUS, MOSAIC].<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Fresh exact verification frame\nThis is chronology-free reentry after construction. It does not assert readiness.\n{\"current_candidate_sha256\":\"82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"current_candidate_version\":\"candidate-v008:82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"full_history_handle\":\"run://2026-08-26-solace-anchored-provenance-interaction-measured-v0/cells/L1_FAULT_TOLERANT_ANCHORED_PROVENANCE\",\"latest_check\":null,\"latest_effect_delivery\":\"visible_in_this_frame\",\"latest_effect_result_id\":\"RESULT-015\",\"schema\":\"solace-verification-current-state-v0\",\"semantic_readiness\":\"not_adjudicated\"}\n--- exact latest admitted effect ---\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v008:82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-015\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"before_sha256\":\"b28d51e6637aa9076e86a3599b5ee1681d64bfc1a37af3ae794a3be81393360b\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v008:82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"cause\":\"actor_replace_decision\",\"changed_file\":\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"prior_check_binding\":null,\"schema\":\"architecture-candidate-effect-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"run_check\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"evaluator:solace-water-evaluator-v1\",\"object_version\":\"82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-016\",\"result_kind\":\"check_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"blocking_requirements\":[\"Q02_hydraulics: missing concepts: 35 psi; three consecutive 30-minute windows | 3 consecutive 30-minute windows\",\"Q03_sampling: missing concepts: forty-eight samples | 48 samples\",\"Q04_pumping: missing concepts: 14.5 mgd; 12.8 mgd; 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent | 10%, 30%, 60%, and 100% | 10/30/60/100 percent; two consecutive 30-minute windows | two 30-minute windows | 2 consecutive 30-minute windows\",\"Q09_observation: missing concepts: 700 milliseconds | 700 ms; 1,200 milliseconds | 1,200 ms | 1200 ms\",\"decision_heading_order: exact ordered level-two headings\"],\"closure_readiness\":\"not_ready\",\"criterion_results\":[{\"criterion_id\":\"Q01_authority\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q02_hydraulics\",\"description\":\"missing concepts: 35 psi; three consecutive 30-minute windows | 3 consecutive 30-minute windows\",\"status\":\"fail\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q03_sampling\",\"description\":\"missing concepts: forty-eight samples | 48 samples\",\"status\":\"fail\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q04_pumping\",\"description\":\"missing concepts: 14.5 mgd; 12.8 mgd; 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent | 10%, 30%, 60%, and 100% | 10/30/60/100 percent; two consecutive 30-minute windows | two 30-minute windows | 2 consecutive 30-minute windows\",\"status\":\"fail\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q05_resources\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q06_treatment\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q07_source\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q08_security\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q09_observation\",\"description\":\"missing concepts: 700 milliseconds | 700 ms; 1,200 milliseconds | 1,200 ms | 1200 ms\",\"status\":\"fail\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q10_environment\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q11_public\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"Q12_currentness\",\"description\":\"task-derived requirement concepts present\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"capacity_sum_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"clock_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"coverage_health_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"decision_heading_order\",\"description\":\"exact ordered level-two headings\",\"status\":\"fail\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"decision_source_breadth\",\"description\":\"12 distinct cited sources\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"decision_title\",\"description\":\"exact decision title\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"decision_word_range\",\"description\":\"word_count=1934; required=1500-2100\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"ledger_heading\",\"description\":\"exact task-native ledger heading\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"ledger_source_breadth\",\"description\":\"14 distinct cited sources\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"power_duration_reversal\",\"description\":\"no unnegated prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"pressure_unit_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"probability_measure_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"self_authorized_readiness\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"threshold_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"}],\"evaluated_candidate_sha256\":\"82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"evaluator_id\":\"solace-water-evaluator-v1\",\"passed\":false,\"raw_result_handle\":\"raw-tool://RESULT-016/evaluator\",\"raw_result_preserved_exactly\":true,\"returncode_class\":\"zero\",\"schema\":\"stable-candidate-bound-check-projection-v1\",\"volatile_fields_excluded\":true}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:BASTION:1-64+CIPHER:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"7a7e4e117076d9f65dc05bb16e1f9557f7de5652de35ef4eef509bc13ffd6631\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-017\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7931}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"source_path\":\"sources/BASTION_HYDRAULICS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f0a85d8273e5058984554a6383d51616f2e103f141b7e268f67215b90fc7ed60\",\"source_size_bytes\":3483,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Hydraulic pressure, storage, and zone isolation evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent minimum distribution pressure is 42 psi in the north zone. The restoration gate is at least 35 psi at every critical node for three consecutive thirty-minute windows; 42 psi must not be converted to 42 kPa or treated as proof of water quality.\nRidge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons. Stored volume and usable treated reserve are different controls.\nA valve map, pump curve, demand allocation, or zone-boundary change makes earlier pressure and residence-time checks stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power. CIPHER sampling locations must follow the current BASTION flow paths.\nMOSAIC rollback is allowed only while the prior valve map remains valid and a current BASTION pressure check passes for the rollback candidate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| HYD-000 | north-zone | v2 | 42.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-001 | south-zone | v2 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-002 | ridge-tank | v2 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-003 | valve-grid | v2 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-004 | north-zone | v2 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-005 | south-zone | v2 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-006 | ridge-tank | v2 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-007 | valve-grid | v2 | 44.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-008 | north-zone | v2 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-009 | south-zone | v2 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-010 | ridge-tank | v2 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-011 | valve-grid | v2 | 43.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-012 | north-zone | v2 | 42.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-013 | south-zone | v2 | 43.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-014 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-015 | valve-grid | v3 | 42.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-016 | north-zone | v3 | 44.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-017 | south-zone | v3 | 42.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-018 | ridge-tank | v3 | 43.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-019 | valve-grid | v3 | 45.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-020 | north-zone | v3 | 43.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-021 | south-zone | v3 | 44.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-022 | ridge-tank | v3 | 42.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-023 | valve-grid | v3 | 44.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-024 | north-zone | v3 | 42.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-025 | south-zone | v3 | 43.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-026 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-027 | valve-grid | v3 | 43.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-028 | north-zone | v4 | 44.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-029 | south-zone | v4 | 42.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-030 | ridge-tank | v4 | 43.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-031 | valve-grid | v4 | 42.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-032 | north-zone | v4 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-033 | south-zone | v4 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-034 | ridge-tank | v4 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-035 | valve-grid | v4 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-036 | north-zone | v4 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-037 | south-zone | v4 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-038 | ridge-tank | v4 | 44.9 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-039 | valve-grid | v4 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-040 | north-zone | v4 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-041 | south-zone | v4 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve psi, gallons, the three-window rule, and candidate currency.\nDistinguish hydraulic service from microbiological and chemical clearance.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CIPHER_LAB.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3991,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current confirmatory set has zero E. coli positives across forty-eight samples. Clearance requires two complete rounds at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient.\nThe benzene reporting limit is 0.5 micrograms per liter and the action threshold is 5.0 micrograms per liter. The reporting limit is not the action threshold and neither is a percent concentration.\nA flow-path, disinfectant-dose, source-water, sampling-plan, or laboratory-method change makes prior samples stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER sample placement consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses. HELIX governs chain of custody and laboratory access.\nAURORA consumes current CIPHER findings for advisory decisions; CIPHER does not itself authorize public restoration.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LAB-000 | entry-point | v2 | 0.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-001 | north-grid | v2 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-002 | south-grid | v2 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-003 | hospital-loop | v2 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-004 | entry-point | v2 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-005 | north-grid | v2 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-006 | south-grid | v2 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-007 | hospital-loop | v2 | 2.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-008 | entry-point | v2 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-009 | north-grid | v2 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-010 | south-grid | v2 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-011 | hospital-loop | v2 | 1.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-012 | entry-point | v2 | 0.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-013 | north-grid | v2 | 1.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-014 | south-grid | v3 | 2.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-015 | hospital-loop | v3 | 0.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-016 | entry-point | v3 | 2.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-017 | north-grid | v3 | 0.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-018 | south-grid | v3 | 1.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-019 | hospital-loop | v3 | 3.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-020 | entry-point | v3 | 1.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-021 | north-grid | v3 | 2.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-022 | south-grid | v3 | 0.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-023 | hospital-loop | v3 | 2.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-024 | entry-point | v3 | 0.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-025 | north-grid | v3 | 1.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-026 | south-grid | v3 | 2.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-027 | hospital-loop | v3 | 1.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-028 | entry-point | v4 | 2.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-029 | north-grid | v4 | 0.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-030 | south-grid | v4 | 1.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-031 | hospital-loop | v4 | 0.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-032 | entry-point | v4 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-033 | north-grid | v4 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-034 | south-grid | v4 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-035 | hospital-loop | v4 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-036 | entry-point | v4 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-037 | north-grid | v4 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-038 | south-grid | v4 | 2.9 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-039 | hospital-loop | v4 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-040 | entry-point | v4 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-041 | north-grid | v4 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve rounds, spacing, sample count, detection limit, action threshold, and staleness.\nState what negative result would falsify clearance and trigger renewed isolation.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:DELTA:1-64+INDIGO:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"c31f85d7dad24e54b12f4b0d24aacfd84098f9663ffb3d67510890c8cf67dda3\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-018\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8171}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/DELTA_PUMPS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"source_size_bytes\":4013,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe treatment works can supply 18 million gallons per day, but the shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 MGD. Pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow.\nThe latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve. A higher stage requires a current candidate-bound pump and pressure test.\nRestoration may advance through 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent demand stages only after two thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION supplies pressure limits, ECHO supplies feeder headroom, and FALCON supplies treatment output. All three constrain DELTA sequencing.\nA pump, valve, main allocation, generator, or treatment-train change makes prior capacity evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PMP-000 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-001 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-002 | booster-east | v2 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-003 | booster-west | v2 | 18.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-004 | pump-1 | v2 | 20.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-005 | pump-2 | v2 | 18.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-006 | booster-east | v2 | 19.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-007 | booster-west | v2 | 20.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-008 | pump-1 | v2 | 19.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-009 | pump-2 | v2 | 20.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-010 | booster-east | v2 | 18.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-011 | booster-west | v2 | 19.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-012 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-013 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-014 | booster-east | v3 | 20.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-015 | booster-west | v3 | 18.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-016 | pump-1 | v3 | 20.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-017 | pump-2 | v3 | 18.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-018 | booster-east | v3 | 19.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-019 | booster-west | v3 | 21.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-020 | pump-1 | v3 | 19.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-021 | pump-2 | v3 | 20.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-022 | booster-east | v3 | 18.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-023 | booster-west | v3 | 20.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-024 | pump-1 | v3 | 18.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-025 | pump-2 | v3 | 19.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-026 | booster-east | v3 | 20.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-027 | booster-west | v3 | 19.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-028 | pump-1 | v4 | 20.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-029 | pump-2 | v4 | 18.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-030 | booster-east | v4 | 19.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-031 | booster-west | v4 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-032 | pump-1 | v4 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-033 | pump-2 | v4 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-034 | booster-east | v4 | 18.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-035 | booster-west | v4 | 20.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-036 | pump-1 | v4 | 18.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-037 | pump-2 | v4 | 19.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-038 | booster-east | v4 | 20.9 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-039 | booster-west | v4 | 19.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-040 | pump-1 | v4 | 20.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-041 | pump-2 | v4 | 18.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve shared capacity, observed flow, stage sequence, windows, and stale conditions.\nDo not infer public-health clearance from hydraulic capacity.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"source_path\":\"sources/INDIGO_TELEMETRY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"64836aa42ff09665cee35507acf1ca8f242ddb78ed4457b0e81e31a93c9c8977\",\"source_size_bytes\":3704,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Telemetry coverage, alerts, and observation quality\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent critical-signal coverage is 96 percent; four percent remains unobserved. Coverage is not confidence and does not prove healthy uninstrumented zones.\nThe warning threshold for pressure is 38 psi and the isolation trigger is 30 psi. Warning and action thresholds must remain distinct.\nTelemetry delay is 700 milliseconds at p95 and 1,200 milliseconds at p99. Both are observations, not control deadlines.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION, DELTA, ECHO, and FALCON rely on INDIGO observations, but each domain retains its own decision gate.\nLUMEN communications may report measured service only where INDIGO coverage and source currency are adequate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| OBS-000 | pressure | v2 | 96.0 | percent-coverage | superseded |\n| OBS-001 | turbidity | v2 | 97.3 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-002 | power | v2 | 98.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-003 | chlorine | v2 | 96.8 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-004 | pressure | v2 | 98.1 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-005 | turbidity | v2 | 96.3 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-006 | power | v2 | 97.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-007 | chlorine | v2 | 98.9 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-008 | pressure | v2 | 97.1 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-009 | turbidity | v2 | 98.4 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-010 | power | v2 | 96.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-011 | chlorine | v2 | 97.9 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-012 | pressure | v2 | 96.1 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-013 | turbidity | v2 | 97.4 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-014 | power | v3 | 98.7 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-015 | chlorine | v3 | 96.9 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-016 | pressure | v3 | 98.2 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-017 | turbidity | v3 | 96.4 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-018 | power | v3 | 97.7 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-019 | chlorine | v3 | 99.0 | percent-coverage | superseded |\n| OBS-020 | pressure | v3 | 97.2 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-021 | turbidity | v3 | 98.5 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-022 | power | v3 | 96.7 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-023 | chlorine | v3 | 98.0 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-024 | pressure | v3 | 96.2 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-025 | turbidity | v3 | 97.5 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-026 | power | v3 | 98.8 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-027 | chlorine | v3 | 97.0 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-028 | pressure | v4 | 98.3 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-029 | turbidity | v4 | 96.5 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-030 | power | v4 | 97.8 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-031 | chlorine | v4 | 96.0 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-032 | pressure | v4 | 97.3 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-033 | turbidity | v4 | 98.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-034 | power | v4 | 96.8 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-035 | chlorine | v4 | 98.1 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-036 | pressure | v4 | 96.3 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-037 | turbidity | v4 | 97.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-038 | power | v4 | 98.9 | percent-coverage | superseded |\n| OBS-039 | chlorine | v4 | 97.1 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-040 | pressure | v4 | 98.4 | percent-coverage | current |\n| OBS-041 | turbidity | v4 | 96.6 | percent-coverage | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve coverage, uncertainty, threshold purpose, percentiles, and units.\nDefine alternate observation routes and evidence for retiring manual watches.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"patch_decision\",\"edits\":[{\"new\":\"The north-zone distribution system currently holds a minimum pressure of 42 psi [BASTION]. The restoration gate requires at least 35 psi at every critical node for three consecutive thirty-minute windows; the current 42 psi reading does not by itself satisfy this multi-window requirement, and psi values must not be converted to kPa or treated as proof of water quality [BASTION]. Ridge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons; these are distinct measures and must not be conflated as treated reserve [BASTION]. DELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power; cavitation constraints limit shared-main capacity under staged demand conditions [DELTA, BASTION, ECHO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states: a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Residence time in the distribution loop must be verified against candidate-bound hydraulic model H12; any change to valve map V8 or controller firmware C11 invalidates prior residence-time evidence [MOSAIC]. The current minimum pressure of 42 psi exceeds the 30 psi isolation trigger but remains within the operational band defined by H12; no isolation action is currently indicated, though the three-consecutive-window restoration gate must still be met before hydraulic clearance can be claimed [BASTION, INDIGO].\",\"old\":\"The north-zone distribution system currently holds a minimum pressure of 42 psi [BASTION]. Ridge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons; these are distinct measures and must not be conflated as treated reserve [BASTION]. DELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power; cavitation constraints limit shared-main capacity under staged demand conditions [DELTA, BASTION, ECHO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states: a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Residence time in the distribution loop must be verified against candidate-bound hydraulic model H12; any change to valve map V8 or controller firmware C11 invalidates prior residence-time evidence [MOSAIC]. The current minimum pressure of 42 psi exceeds the 30 psi isolation trigger but remains within the operational band defined by H12; no isolation action is currently indicated [BASTION, INDIGO].\"},{\"new\":\"Clearance requires two complete sampling rounds spaced at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient. The current confirmatory set comprises forty-eight samples with zero E. coli positives across all locations [CIPHER].\",\"old\":\"Clearance requires two complete sampling rounds spaced at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient [CIPHER].\"},{\"new\":\"Emergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock; the duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load [ECHO]. The grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW; rated power is not usable power [ECHO]. KESTREL diesel stock covers emergency load for 36 hours and full pump load for 22 hours; these load regimes are distinct and must not be merged as a single duration [KESTREL, ECHO]. Coagulant and chlorine chemical stocks provide 4.5 days and 3.2 days of treatment capacity respectively; inventory duration is not delivery lead time [KESTREL, FALCON]. Staffing continuity depends on mutual-aid logistics; current shift coverage must be verified against the 36-hour generator window [KESTREL]. Any change to ECHO power state or KESTREL fuel stock makes prior pump sequencing evidence stale [DELTA, ECHO, KESTREL]. The shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 million gallons per day, and pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow; the latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve [DELTA]. Restoration may advance through ten, thirty, sixty, and one hundred percent demand stages only after two consecutive thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates [DELTA]. The shared-main limit under staged demand requires that DELTA pump capacity not exceed the 6.5 MW usable grid feed plus any available generator margin without triggering cavitation constraints [DELTA, ECHO, BASTION].\",\"old\":\"Emergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock; the duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load [ECHO]. The grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW; rated power is not usable power [ECHO]. KESTREL diesel stock covers emergency load for 36 hours and full pump load for 22 hours; these load regimes are distinct and must not be merged as a single duration [KESTREL, ECHO]. Coagulant and chlorine chemical stocks provide 4.5 days and 3.2 days of treatment capacity respectively; inventory duration is not delivery lead time [KESTREL, FALCON]. Staffing continuity depends on mutual-aid logistics; current shift coverage must be verified against the 36-hour generator window [KESTREL]. Any change to ECHO power state or KESTREL fuel stock makes prior pump sequencing evidence stale [DELTA, ECHO, KESTREL]. The shared-main limit under staged demand requires that DELTA pump capacity not exceed the 6.5 MW usable grid feed plus any available generator margin without triggering cavitation constraints [DELTA, ECHO, BASTION].\"},{\"new\":\"Critical-signal telemetry coverage stands at 96 percent, with 4 percent of monitored points unobserved; this coverage gap does not prove the uninstrumented zones are healthy, only that they are not currently observable [INDIGO]. Telemetry delay is 700 milliseconds at p95 and 1,200 milliseconds at p99; both are observations, not control deadlines [INDIGO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states; a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Telemetry delays in the unobserved 4 percent create uncertainty that must be treated as potential adverse condition until verified by direct observation or alternate telemetry [INDIGO]. Warnings versus actions: a pressure warning at 38 psi requires monitoring and logging but does not require isolation; an isolation trigger at 30 psi requires immediate valve closure and zone separation [INDIGO, BASTION]. Any change to hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, or control-system key set W4 invalidates prior telemetry correlation evidence and requires re-verification of coverage and alert thresholds [MOSAIC, INDIGO, BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON]. Alternate telemetry paths must be identified for the 4 percent unobserved zone before closure can be claimed [INDIGO, NEXUS].\",\"old\":\"Critical-signal telemetry coverage stands at 96 percent, with 4 percent of monitored points unobserved; this coverage gap does not prove the uninstrumented zones are healthy, only that they are not currently observable [INDIGO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states; a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Telemetry delays in the unobserved 4 percent create uncertainty that must be treated as potential adverse condition until verified by direct observation or alternate telemetry [INDIGO]. Warnings versus actions: a pressure warning at 38 psi requires monitoring and logging but does not require isolation; an isolation trigger at 30 psi requires immediate valve closure and zone separation [INDIGO, BASTION]. Any change to hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, or control-system key set W4 invalidates prior telemetry correlation evidence and requires re-verification of coverage and alert thresholds [MOSAIC, INDIGO, BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON]. Alternate telemetry paths must be identified for the 4 percent unobserved zone before closure can be claimed [INDIGO, NEXUS].\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v009:56dbd283bef7636af26b7cad3d0fcbf11b3b6421664fb77dee67cced063e254d\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-019\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha25